 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Part numbering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Base part number SS10P3 or SS10P4 sets the reverse voltage. Suffix -M3 is the halogen-free, RoHS-compliant commercial grade; HM3_X is halogen-free, RoHS-compliant and AEC-Q101 qualified, where X is a revision letter (A, B, ...). After the slash comes the packing code: 86A or H for 7-inch reels of 1500, 87A or I for 13-inch reels of 6500."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Single Schottky barrier junction with a guard ring for overvoltage protection, in the eSMP-series SMPC (TO-277A) case of about 1.1 mm typical height. Molding compound rated UL 94 V-0. Leads are matte tin, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD 22-B102; both M3 and HM3 versions pass the JESD 201 class 2 whisker test. Moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With a resistive or inductive load and the lead temperature taken at the cathode band terminal, the full 10 A average holds up to about 127 °C lead temperature and falls in a straight line to zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Junction-to-lead resistance is 3 °C/W typical; junction-to-ambient is 60 °C/W typical on the recommended pad layout with 1 oz copper. The transient thermal impedance to ambient rises from about 6 °C/W at 10 ms pulses to about 60 °C/W at 100 s."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Applications",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Uses given: low-voltage high-frequency inverters, freewheeling, DC/DC converters and polarity protection."
  }
 ],
